const faqs = [
    {
        q: "How often should engine oil be changed in Dubai?",
        a: "Engine oil change intervals depend primarily on your vehicle manufacturer's recommendations, the type of oil used, and your driving conditions. In Dubai, frequent idling in traffic, short trips, and high summer temperatures classify most daily driving as 'severe service'. Under these conditions, fully synthetic oil is typically changed every 8,000 to 10,000 km (or within 6 to 12 months), semi-synthetic blends around 6,000 to 7,500 km, and conventional mineral oils every 5,000 km. Always consult your vehicle's handbook for exact guidelines."
    },
    {
        q: "What is the best engine oil for driving in Dubai's heat?",
        a: "The best oil is the exact viscosity grade and quality specification mandated by your vehicle manufacturer. Modern engines often require low-viscosity synthetic oils like 0W-20 or 5W-30 with specific manufacturer approvals (such as BMW Longlife, Mercedes-Benz 229.5, or VW 504/507), while other vehicles may specify 5W-40 or 10W-40. Our mechanics verify your engine's technical requirements before adding oil to ensure proper lubrication and thermal stability."
