    },
    {
        q: "How does independent garage servicing compare to fuel-station lube bays?",
        a: "While fuel-station bays often use top-side dipstick suction to remove oil quickly, our workshop raises vehicles on two-post hydraulic hoists for thorough gravity draining from the oil pan sump plug. In addition, our mechanics take the time to inspect visible underbody components—including the oil pan, steering rack, suspension bushings, and brake lines—for early signs of wear or fluid leakage."
    },
    {
        q: "What happens if the wrong oil viscosity or specification is used?",
